  "solution": "The logic followed here is,\n\nLogic: **Second no. = [(First no. + Third no.) × 10]**\n\n(16, 350, 19) →\n\n⇒ [ (16 + 19) × 10]\n\n⇒ (35 × 10) = 350\n\n(14, 310, 17) →\n\n⇒ [ (14 + 17) × 10]\n\n⇒ (31 × 10) = 310\n\nChecking all the given options:\n\n**1. (17, 380, 19) →**\n\n⇒ [ (17 + 19) × 10]\n\n⇒ (36 × 10) = 360\n\n**2. (12, 300, 19) →**\n\n⇒ [ (12 + 19) × 10]\n\n⇒ (31 × 10) = 310\n\n**3. (12, 240, 17) →**\n\n⇒ [ (12 + 17) × 10]\n\n⇒ (29 × 10) = 290\n\n**4. (13, 320, 19) →**\n\n⇒ **[ (13 + 19) × 10]**\n\n**⇒ (32 × 10) =** **320**\n\nHere, (13, 320, 19) is showing a similar relation to the given set of numbers.\n\nHence, the correct answer is \"**(13, 320, 19)**\".",
